0..43 Comment "// This source models short string storage."
44..46 Comment "//"
47..123 Comment "// A short string stores its bytes inline. It uses no allocation through the"
124..199 Comment "// inline capacity. A long string stores bytes in a heap buffer. Both forms"
200..225 Comment "// expose the same bytes."
226..228 Comment "//"
229..306 Comment "// `store` selects the location. `own` stores code points as bytes and adds a"
307..315 Comment "// zero."
316..318 Comment "//"
319..351 Comment "// - see: #1481 — `repeatOnto`"
352..414 Comment "// - see: libc++ `std::string` — small-string representation"
415..477 Comment "// - see: Rust `compact_str` — inline 24-byte representation"
479..546 Comment "// This source imports declarations for lists, bytes and ownership."
